  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4{a}^{3}(2{a}^{4}{b}^{2}+3{a}^{2}+2) & = \\\\ (-4{a}^{3})(2{a}^{4}{b}^{2})+(-4{a}^{3})(3{a}^{2})+(-4{a}^{3})(2) & = \\\\ (-8)({a}^{3+4})({b}^{2})+(-12)({a}^{3+2})+(-8)({a}^{3}) & = \\\\ -8{a}^{7}{b}^{2}-12{a}^{5}-8{a}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
